WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:20.620
Beloved class of 2021,

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.957
I stand here in
awe of you.

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:26.459
Right now,
this celebration is what

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:29.929
Benedictine nun and spiritual
writer Joan Chittister would

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.799
call a "firework moment".

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:36.036
Your accomplishments
both within and outside of your

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:40.340
fields of study, extend far
beyond formal measure.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.443
There were likely times leading
up to this day when you felt

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:46.112
broken or without hope.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:49.449
There might have been times
when you could not imagine how

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.818
to find your way through
to the end.

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:56.890
And yet here you are,
a fuller and deeper you.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.460
Although this day is not what
any of us thought it would be

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:04.831
when you began this journey,
even if bittersweet in part,

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.033
it is a day to be cherished.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:11.271
You are to be cherished.
In the uncertainty, in the

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:14.908
hard work, in the
failures and in the thriving,

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:18.945
you have persisted through
it all, and today you must

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:22.715
allow yourself
to simply sparkle.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:28.721
And now, my beloved Yale family,
wherever you might be, I invite

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.891
you to join me
in the spirit of prayer,

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.295
Almighty and Loving Creator,

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:39.466
You are the Force that lights
the stars. The Architect of

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:43.336
every cell, the Source
of all Truth.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:46.306
We look to you
as many expressions of one

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:49.976
living mystery, a mystery
beyond all telling.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:54.647
In this moment, we are people
grieving many different types

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:59.285
of losses, and our hearts beat
with the rhythm of lament as we

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:02.522
cope with emotions too
complex for any of us

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.424
to fully understand.

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:09.896
We who share this beautiful but
aching world, we who look at the

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:13.766
same sun and the same
moon are of people called

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.202
to communal restoration.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:19.839
As students of your handiwork,
we gathered at Yale from

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:23.143
throughout the Earth with
exquisite ambitions and have

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:26.546
been blessed at this place of
light and truth with the

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:31.784
freedom to let them grow.
Our God of all generations.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:35.255
You are the guardian of where
we are going and who

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:36.789
we are becoming.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:39.926
We are filled with gratitude
for our families, friends,

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.694
teachers and guides.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:44.998
Their arms have sheltered us,
their shoulders have

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:49.836
boosted us, and today their
hearts are holding fast to us.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:54.274
Bless us as we seek to
reimagine a world made better

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:57.877
by the considerable gifts we
will now bring to it.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:02.282
May we exude an intelligence
that is inspired by justice,

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:05.885
guided by tenderness,
moved by holiness,

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:09.022
and always informed by love.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:14.561
As we greet tomorrow, steady us
on solid ground and together

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:21.401
may we become vibrant living
examples of shalom, of salaam,

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:24.370
of shanti, of peace.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.974
Let us say Amen.

